cff-version: 1.2.0
title: gp_dla_finder
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the method papers below. A software
  citation is in preparation; until it exists, cite the method papers and note
  the software version used.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ming-Feng
    family-names: Ho
    email: mfho@umich.edu
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4457-890X"
    affiliation: >-
      Leinweber Center for Theoretical Physics, University of Michigan
repository-code: "https://github.com/jibanCat/gp_dla_finder"
abstract: >-
  Gaussian-process Bayesian detection of damped Lyman-alpha absorbers in quasar
  spectra. Packages the inference core of the DESI GP-DLA finder for use on a
  single spectrum, independently of any survey production pipeline. Lower
  column-density absorbers are included in the inference prior for
  regularization, but are not independently validated catalogue targets.
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - cosmology
  - quasar
  - damped Lyman-alpha
  - Gaussian process
  - spectroscopy
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0rc3
references:
  # --- method papers -------------------------------------------------------
  - type: article
    title: Detecting Damped Lyman-alpha Absorbers with Gaussian Processes
    authors:
      - family-names: Garnett
        given-names: Roman
      - family-names: Ho
        given-names: Shirley
      - family-names: Bird
        given-names: Simeon
      - family-names: Schneider
        given-names: Jeff
    journal: Monthly Notices of the Royal Astronomical Society
    year: 2017
    doi: 10.1093/mnras/stx1958
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/1605.04460"
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Detecting Multiple DLAs per Spectrum in SDSS DR12 with Gaussian Processes
    authors:
      - family-names: Ho
        given-names: Ming-Feng
      - family-names: Bird
        given-names: Simeon
      - family-names: Garnett
        given-names: Roman
    journal: Monthly Notices of the Royal Astronomical Society
    year: 2020
    doi: 10.1093/mnras/staa1806
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2003.11036"
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Damped Lyman-alpha Absorbers from Sloan Digital Sky Survey DR16Q with
      Gaussian processes
    authors:
      - family-names: Ho
        given-names: Ming-Feng
      - family-names: Bird
        given-names: Simeon
      - family-names: Garnett
        given-names: Roman
    journal: Monthly Notices of the Royal Astronomical Society
    year: 2021
    doi: 10.1093/mnras/stab2169
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2103.10964"
  # --- provenance of the bundled default trained model ---------------------
  # Preprint as of 2026-08-18, submitted to A&A. No journal DOI has been
  # invented; update this entry if a published version appears.
  - type: article
    title: >-
      CoLoRe-2LPT: Lyman-alpha mock catalogues for the validation of DESI
      cosmological analyses
    authors:
      - family-names: Ruiz-Herrera Bernal
        given-names: M. F.
    year: 2026
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.27412"
    notes: >-
      Describes the Lyman-alpha mock used to train the bundled default model.
      Cite when using that model. See NOTICE.md.
